{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368199-shot-with-the-firearm-against","id":1368199,"title":"Shot with the firearm against","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T19:12:57-08:00","id":1368199,"title":"Shot with the firearm against","content":"First of all, I'm sorry if the subject has been discussed previously.<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this situation?<br /> My character manages to put the firearm against the target and threatens, and will pull the trigger at any moment if the target moves.<br /> The target moves and my character pulls the trigger with the gun leaning against the target.<br /> What is your opinion for the test to be done?<br /> Subtract defense in the firearm test?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T19:47:09-08:00","id":1368209,"title":"","content":"So for the shooting part itself:<br /> <br /> Unless there are any applicable Merits/powers/etc. modifying things, in close range there's a limited way to apply Defense against firearms: if the firearm is larger than Size 1 (which means anything bigger than a pistol), there target gets a Defense of (weapons Size + 1).<br /> <br /> So, if your character is using a revolver, the target gets no Defense even in close range.<br /> <br /> If your character is using a shotgun, the target gets a Defense of 3.<br /> <br /> And you resolve the shot per the normal rules otherwise. In this case, I'd presume that your character has delayed their action for this.<br /> <br /> You could consider a social roll to threaten the target, depending on how things are going, and modify the target's actions based on the quality of the threat roll. If you character is trying to get the target to do something specific, your ST might call for a Forcing Doors roll (from the Social Maneuvering system) to make this a bit tougher than a normal intimidation check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T22:32:38-08:00","id":1368225,"title":"","content":"Depending on how important the NPC is to my purposes.... If the NPC isn't very important to anything I've planned.... Or is more just a mortal or not very skilled... I'd probably let the PC just execute the person and have them deal with the fallout of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T01:13:09-08:00","id":1368240,"title":"","content":"To be a bit more clear in addition to that. When I said I'd resolve the shot per the normal rules, I mean to include the decision to use the Down &amp; Dirty Combat rules or the full Combat rules as the case would entail. I might not just have an NPC auto-killed if they can react to something, but a minor NPC would probably be looking at a single roll rather than the whole deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T02:17:49-08:00","id":1368255,"title":"","content":"It could also use the firing Vs a incapacitated person and the person gets full dicepool successes. It's basically the same as putting a gun right up to a sleeping person and firing, anything bar supernatural defense and they should get blammed hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:46:46-08:00","id":1368620,"title":"","content":"I would treat it like a coup de grace, or a 'killing blow' as Chronicles of Darkness calls it. This means you look at the amount of dice you would normally roll for your attack, and then you automatically do that amount of damage plus the weapon modifier rating. <br /> <br /> So if you put a gun to someone's head and you perform a killing bow (which is what I would allow in this situation) and you have a Dexterity of 3, a Firearms of 3 and you're using a light pistol, you do 3+3+1=7 lethal damage, which is probably enough to just instantly kill the person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T13:17:01-08:00","id":1368625,"title":"","content":"You better spend WP, since Stamina 3+ means 7 damage isn't enough to even KO someone, let alone instantly kill them.<br /> <br /> Killing Blow works well for what it's stated intention is: attacking incapacitated or immobile targets.<br /> <br /> If you want to get an instant kill ASAP mechanically, the Down &amp; Dirty rules are the fastest way towards that end (in terms of applying the rules) since if your intention is to murder someone, and you win the roll, they die.<br /> <br /> Putting a gun against a target that still has the ability to move around means they can try to get away from you. While dangerous and requiring significant training to realistically have a chance of doing (yay Merits...), there are real world combat techniques for disarming someone that's pointing a gun at you at the ranges we're discussing. In fact they rely on the person with the gun getting too close instead of staying back a few yards.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say you need to break out the whole combat system, or even roll at all and not just say the shooter kills the target, but that should be a ST decision based on the context of the scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T19:36:47-08:00","id":1368667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368199-shot-with-the-firearm-against?p=1368625#post1368625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting a gun against a target that still has the ability to move around means they can try to get away from you. While dangerous and requiring significant training to realistically have a chance of doing (yay Merits...), there are real world combat techniques for disarming someone that's pointing a gun at you at the ranges we're discussing. In fact they rely on the person with the gun getting too close instead of staying back a few yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obligatory Kiss Kiss Bang Bang reference:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6svL10xXulQ\" data-code=\"6svL10xXulQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6svL10xXulQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T11:47:30-08:00","id":1368781,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all partipation! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will highlight the following, my character postponed the action with the trigger to fire the firearm in case the target moves - both were stopped.<br /> <br /> After thinking about intimidation and considering that I was unable to intimidate, the best test to do is whether my character can perceive the target's movement to shoot, with a Stealth vs perception test. Remembering that the aggressor can distract with something and give the breach. Successfully Stealth test, the victim is able to act before the shot and has a chance to get rid of it.<br /> In the end, in common situations, I would do tests favoring the aggressor with a firearm leaning against the target, but I do not eliminate the victim's chance to defend himself.<br /> <br /> The films generally do not represent very well an interpretive combat either, because the good guys do whatever they want making the most improbabilities happen. I'm thinking about relatively common characters.<br /> <br /> If the target is an important NPC I consider the test Dexterit + Weaponry to lean the gun!<br /> <br /> I apply the defense against firearms (rules for close combat with gun) if the character with the firearm is attacked in hand-to-hand combat before acting, then having difficulties to aim the weapon at his very close attacker.<br /> <br /> What intrigued me in the game I participated in was the storytelling using rules from the D&amp;D 3.0 / 3.5 board for the game and told me that shooting from 2 meters away is considered point blank shot.<br /> D&amp;D is a fun game, but the rules of the board for combat are not suitable for an interpretive action scene from the Chronicle of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","user":"BrunoMoonChangeling","date":". 02-18-2020, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T04:34:10-08:00","id":1369122,"title":"","content":"I think a straight initiative roll works well here; it's a situation almost entirely dependent on who has faster reflexes. If the PC wins they see the target start to move and fire, if the NPC wins they can attempt a grapple and then go for a control weapon move. <br /> <br /> Assuming the NPC is a pretty average person it's risky because they need to win several rolls in order to reverse the situation: Initiative-&gt;grapple-&gt;control weapon-&gt;damage. Without an exceptional success it takes a couple turns of struggling for a normal person to wrestle a gun away and use it on their assailant; the slick instant disarm moves are, as noted, the purview of merits representing extensive training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:07:06-08:00","id":1369171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368199-shot-with-the-firearm-against?p=1369122#post1369122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a straight initiative roll works well here; it's a situation almost entirely dependent on who has faster reflexes. If the PC wins they see the target start to move and fire, if the NPC wins they can attempt a grapple and then go for a control weapon move. <br /> <br /> Assuming the NPC is a pretty average person it's risky because they need to win several rolls in order to reverse the situation: Initiative-&gt;grapple-&gt;control weapon-&gt;damage. Without an exceptional success it takes a couple turns of struggling for a normal person to wrestle a gun away and use it on their assailant; the slick instant disarm moves are, as noted, the purview of merits representing extensive training.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that represents very well the difficulty of reacting against someone armed.<br /> Thinking on basic rules only, without Merit or Supernatural, an aggressor with a firearm often have the advantage, the victim who needs to have a differential or a lot of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T20:52:50-07:00","id":1376362,"title":"","content":"The Exalted 3rd Edition had detailed Hold at Bay combat options.<br /> <br /> Knife to the neck<br /> Gun to the torso<br /> <br /> Interesting read, would be nice to see a CoD conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}